<title>USA: Young Broadcasting to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>Young Broadcasting to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Young Broadcasting Inc said on Monday that its board approved the initiation of an ongoing stock buyback program for up to $20 million of the company's class A common stock.</p>
<p>The company said its common stock represents an attractive value at its current price and it will evaluate the market price in determining when to buy back shares.</p>
<p>Young Broadcasting currently owns 12 television stations.  </p>
<p>Young Broadcasting has about 14.2 million shares outstanding, a company spokesman said.</p>
</text>
